course: dictionary
lesson: 5753
title: Lower: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «Lower» can mean less high, smaller, at the bottom, or to make something less. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: «Research suggests time outdoors in daylight lowers the risk of children becoming short-sighted.» Here lowers means makes less. Test it: put make less in place of lowers, and the sentence still makes sense. Short-sighted is a hard word, but you can read on, because the sentence is about risk.
explain: «To tell them apart, look at the snout and the teeth: an alligator has a wide U-shaped snout and its lower teeth hide when it shuts its mouth.» Here lower means the bottom ones, the teeth at the bottom of the mouth. The word teeth and the word mouth give you the clue about position.
explain: Lower can also be a doing word, a verb. «Missing payments lowers a credit score» means makes it less. When you are not sure which meaning fits, try each one in the sentence. A dictionary can settle it if the clues are not enough.
fact: Lower is an adjective when it means less high, smaller, or at the bottom, as in «lower teeth».
fact: Lower is a verb when it means to move something down or to make it less, as in «lowers the risk».
fact: «Lower case» letters are the small letters, such as a, b and c. «Capital» letters are the big ones.
fact: In a river, the lower part is the part nearest the sea.
fact: To lower a price, a sound or a voice means to make it less.
exercise: «Time outdoors lowers the risk of children becoming short-sighted.» What does lowers mean here? | Moves something to the ground | Gives out light | *Makes less | Makes louder
exercise: In maths, 5 is lower than 8. What does lower mean here? | *Smaller | Brighter | Higher | Louder
exercise: Mum says, «Lower your voice, please.» What should you do? | *Speak more quietly | Shout | Move your voice to the top of the stairs | Sing a higher note
test: «Shops lower prices in a sale.» What does lower mean here? | Move up | Make bigger | *Make less | Put in a box
test: Which of these is a lower case letter? | *c | Z | M | A
exam: «The lower part of a river is near the sea.» In this sentence, what does lower mean? | Bigger than the top part | Higher up in the hills | Louder than the rest | *At the bottom, nearest the sea
